# Flash Sale: project rules

## Scope
- Always read @TASK.md and @ARCHITECTURE.md before working. Do not add functionality outside them.

## Data and concurrency
- Stock and sale status change ONLY inside `prisma.$transaction` after `SELECT ... FROM "Sale" WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE` on the Sale row. Never "read, then update" in two separate queries.
- Money is stored in cents (integers).
- Time is passed as a `now` parameter into service and ticker functions so tests can control it. Do not call `new Date()` / `Date.now()` inside business logic.

## Tests
- Write the test first, then the implementation.
- Concurrency tests must use `Promise.all` with real parallel requests.
- Do not skip failing tests (no `.skip`, `.only`, `.todo`, or commented-out tests to make a run green).

## Working process
- Work in small steps. After each step: run the tests, and only if they pass, update DECISIONS.md and make a git commit.
- At the end of every step, append a DECISIONS.md entry for each non-obvious choice made during that step (library, schema change, deviation from ARCHITECTURE.md), and a "Known issues / not done" line if anything was skipped.
- If you deviate from ARCHITECTURE.md, update ARCHITECTURE.md in the same commit and say so in the DECISIONS.md entry and in the commit message body.
- Timestamps in DECISIONS.md and AI_LOG.md must come from the terminal command `date "+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %z"` (numeric offset like `+0600`, not a zone name). Never invent a time. In PowerShell `date` is an alias of `Get-Date`, so call Git's binary: `& "C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin\date.exe" "+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %z"`.

## Git
- Do not rewrite git history (no `commit --amend`, `rebase`, `reset --hard`, or force push).
- Commit messages use the format `type: short description`, where type is one of `feat`, `fix`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`.
